/* CORRECTED R2 on the REAL model (sweep.py / Conventions sec.12), replacing the
 * classical-pendulum |M|=Vg.  The real GFL loses its operating equilibrium via a
 * SADDLE-NODE (voltage collapse) when the vcd-equilibrium quadratic loses its real
 * roots.  Equilibrium relations (sweep.py lines 13-15, iqr=0):
 *     cos(th) = (al*vcd - K1)/Vg,   sin(th) = (K2 - be*vcd)/Vg,
 *     al = 1 - wn^2*Lg*Cf,  be = Rg*wn*Cf,  K1 = Rg*idr,  K2 = wn*Lg*idr.
 * cos^2+sin^2=1  =>  a2*vcd^2 + a1*vcd + a0 = 0  with the REAL coefficients
 *     a2 = al^2 + be^2,   a1 = -2*Rg*idr,   a0 = Lg^2*idr^2*wn^2 + Rg^2*idr^2 - Vg^2.
 * (a1 simplifies: the Cf terms in al*K1+be*K2 cancel, leaving al*K1+be*K2 = Rg*idr.)
 * Fold surface = discriminant disc = a1^2 - 4*a2*a0 = 0.  Located numerically at
 * SCR*~0.370 (Lg*~0.0124 H) -- a genuine saddle-node (the two vcd equilibria merge).
 * This is DEEPER weak-grid than the PLL-mode Hopf (SCR_H~0.905), which binds first.
 * Unlike the retracted classical |M|=Vg, every coefficient here is the real sweep.py
 * coefficient.  This entry: a2 = al^2+be^2 > 0 for physical params, so it is a real
 * quadratic (not degenerate). */
Problem
  \forall wn \forall Rg \forall Cf \forall Lg
  ( wn>0 & Rg>0 & Cf>0 -> (1 - wn^2*Lg*Cf)^2 + (Rg*wn*Cf)^2 > 0 )
End.
Tactic "a2>0 by QE"
  QE
End.
End. """"
  tactic """" QE """"
  proof """"  """"
End.
